  ],
  "why": "Sizes imply a range: a film that never leaves medium shots feels polite, and one that only erupts into close-ups spends them cheaply — while the insert (the ticking clock, the dripping tap) is the ladder's editorial workhorse."
};

const scgScarcityPredict = {
